MFS --point-sources now runs on the streamed path: no visibilities held.
Every term a point column needs is a value of the w-tilde kernel K(lag) or
the data's dirty image Dd(x) (Gaussian widths are convolutions of those),
so the streaming pass accumulates both on grids 8x finer than the image and
streamed_points.StreamedAugmentedSystem reads them by quintic spline
(2e-9 of the peak). Fits match the in-memory system: same detections,
fluxes to 1e-6.

The streaming pass now uses batched type-1 NUFFTs instead of a per-chunk
DFT (45 us/sample at 112x112 against 2.4 ms; ~98 us with the point grids).

SparseMesh.cross_on_grid builds (W~ M)^T in column batches: autoarray's
single call needed ~5 GB of FFT transients on Teresa's grid (OOM here,
likely swap on her laptop). Same numbers to the bit.

The point stage is factored out of run() into _point_stage, shared with
run_streamed. Cube mode with points still runs in memory.

